I was dismayed to find that I couldn't #rub my magic whistle today. Why
not? I think #rub should be extended to let you try rubbing anything in
your inventory you'd like to rub, except that it just gives you a silly
message for anything uninteresting.

There could be entertaining side effects. Maybe you could get splinters
from rubbing wooden things, your dexterity could go down temporarily,
similar to how your leg hurts after having kicked a wall. If you rub a
potion of oil maybe you'd get greasy fingers. If you rub a bladed
weapon you get a cut and lose 1-2 HP. If you rub a scroll you might
have a chance of rubbing the words out and it turning into blank paper.

You could even rub ".": "You rub yourself. You feel tense." That might
be difficult because it's a direction, not an inventory item, though.

The possibilities are endless.



